      "notes": "NIK 2025, OTR Jakarta Rp3,429,000,000 (off-the-road Rp3,401,000,000), unchanged June 2026. Two-tone exterior version has the same specs: OTR Rp3,576,000,000 (NIK 2024). Earlier OTR: Rp3,330,000,000 (July 2024), Rp3,415,000,000 (June 2025). Battery left out: the bmw.co.id technical page prints 81.2 kWh, which looks copied from the i5 (global i7 xDrive60 is about 101.7 kWh net). Torque conflict: BMW Indonesia 745 Nm vs detikOto 2023 launch report 795 Nm. Range: technical page 515-624 km WLTP; detik quoted 590-625 km. AC 11 kW standard, 22 kW optional. Drive, connectors, seats, airbags (7) and ADAS from the Malaysian spec (paultan.org, carbase.my); gross/usable battery (105.7/101.7 kWh), chemistry, voltage, charge port, V2L, frunk and heat pump from the European spec (ev-database.org).",
      "notes_id": "NIK 2025, OTR Jakarta Rp3.429.000.000 (off-the-road Rp3.401.000.000), tidak berubah per Juni 2026. Versi eksterior two-tone memiliki spesifikasi sama: OTR Rp3.576.000.000 (NIK 2024). OTR sebelumnya: Rp3.330.000.000 (Juli 2024), Rp3.415.000.000 (Juni 2025). Baterai dikosongkan: halaman teknis bmw.co.id mencantumkan 81,2 kWh, yang tampaknya tersalin dari i5 (i7 xDrive60 global sekitar 101,7 kWh net). Torsi berbeda: BMW Indonesia 745 Nm vs laporan peluncuran detikOto 2023 795 Nm. Jarak tempuh: halaman teknis 515-624 km WLTP; detik menyebut 590-625 km. AC 11 kW standar, 22 kW opsional. Penggerak, konektor, jumlah kursi, airbag (7), dan ADAS dari spesifikasi Malaysia (paultan.org, carbase.my); baterai gross/usable (105,7/101,7 kWh), kimia baterai, tegangan, posisi port, V2L, frunk, dan heat pump dari spesifikasi Eropa (ev-database.org)."
